From ae7290882a801b6480334f85793887abc2f5eb8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yohan <you@example.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 04:54:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Frontend: fix email selection/navigation ID normalization
 bugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: EmailTable.tsx sourced its rows from the static mockEmails
dataset instead of the live availableEmails list from ActiveCaseContext.
Every page built on InvestigationWorkspace/EmailTable (Investigation hub,
Forensics, Indicators, Infrastructure, AI Investigation, Reports) was
therefore selecting/investigating mock IDs that don't exist in the
backend, causing unreliable single-click previews, 404s on double-click,
and unreliable Last Viewed updates.

Fixes:
- EmailTable.tsx: source rows from useActiveCase().availableEmails
  instead of the mock dataset (the one shared-layer fix that cascades
  correctly to every page using it)
- IndicatorsPage.tsx, InfrastructurePage.tsx, AIInvestigationPage.tsx:
  replaced fabricated { id, subject, caseId } stub objects with
  getEmail(activeEmailData.emailId) from availableEmails, so
  InvestigationShell/CaseSelector always receive a real, complete
  ScannedEmail (or null, rendered safely) instead of an incomplete
  object missing .status/.sender/.date/.threatScore (was causing a
  black screen once a detail view loaded)
- InvestigationWorkspace.tsx (EmailPreview): default .indicators and
  .whyFlagged to [] so a lightweight/partial record can't crash the
  shared preview
- api.ts (getEmail): guard against undefined/null/empty-string/non-
  string emailId, throwing a clear error instead of silently hitting
  GET /api/v1/emails/undefined
- OverviewPage.tsx: added the missing onDoubleClick handler on table
  rows (reusing the existing handleInspect navigation — no new
  navigation system), since Overview previously had no double-click
  behavior at all

No backend changes, no API contract changes, no mock-data introduced,
no UI redesign, no changes to the AI/ML availability contract.

npm run build: clean.
